COMMON TRAPS

- ⚠️ Potentials in Medium: Remember that K (dielectric) reduces potential; divide by K.
- ⚠️ Sign of Charge: NEVER forget to put the (+) or (-) sign of q in potential/potential energy formulas.
- ⚠️ Shell Potential: Many mistakenly think V = 0 inside a hollow shell. Field is 0, but Potential is constant (kQ/R).
- ⚠️ Dipole Force: F = 0 only in UNIFORM fields. If field is non-uniform, F ≠ 0.
- ⚠️ Earthing vs Charge: Earthing makes V = 0. The conductor can still hold charge if other charges are nearby.
- ⚠️ Energy Calculation: Total energy is the sum of ALL individual U_self and ALL U_interaction pairs.
- ⚠️ Work Done: Check if question asks for work by "Electric Field" ( -ΔU ) or "External Agent" ( ΔU ).
- ⚠️ Dipole Direction: p is always from negative charge to positive charge.

